{
  "info": {
    "name": "Auth API",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the Express + MySQL auth API.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start the API (`npm run dev`) and seed it (`npm run db:seed`).\n2. Check the collection variables: `baseUrl`, and the seeded `adminEmail` / `userEmail` / `password`.\n3. Run **Auth → Login (user)** or **Login (admin)** first. It saves `accessToken`, which every protected request sends as a Bearer token (set once on the collection).\n\n**Refresh token.** It comes back only as an httpOnly `refreshToken` cookie scoped to `/api/auth`. Postman keeps it in its cookie jar and sends it on Refresh / Logout automatically. The login scripts also copy it into the `refreshToken` variable for the body-based refresh request.\n\n**Email tokens.** Verification and reset links are printed in the server console when SMTP is not configured. Copy the `token=` value from the link into the `verifyToken` or `resetToken` variable.\n\n**Rate limits.** 5 failed logins per 15 minutes per IP and email; 3 verification/reset emails per hour per IP and email.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
